## Rules for a connector

- Fixtures are invented. Never commit a captured response (not trimmed, not "anonymised"), a token, a
  cookie or an account.
- Nothing is evaded: no anti-detection flags, no user-agent or IP rotation, no CAPTCHA solving, no
  reverse-engineering of request signatures. Back off on 429 (the shared client does). If the service
  wants a person, a person logs in.
- Use the shared `HttpClient` through `catalog_sync.sdk.Connection`: it holds the pace the
  compliance block declares. Do not write your own request loop.
- Fail honestly: `AuthExpired` for a rejected credential, `ItemFailed` for one bad item,
  `SourceShapeError` for an answer of the wrong shape; a value you cannot understand is `None` plus
  a note in `issues`, never a guess.

The full guide, including what the SDK cannot do (request signing computed in JavaScript, pages that
are only HTML), is `docs/connector-guide.md` in the catalog-sync repository.
